# SFT execution status v0.116

2026-09-26. The generation-stable child ownership and reap primitive for the
write-guard process composition is implemented and locally verified. **This
closes the pidfd child-lifecycle design primitive, but it does not fork or run
the process composition; Gate 5 remains incomplete.** No real process, signal,
waitid, pidfd, socket, cgroup, listener, payload, remote mutation, GPU
operation, inference or training occurred.

## Completed

- A fresh numeric child PID is used exactly once for `pidfd_open`. All later
  liveness, termination, wait, reap and close operations are bound to the
  resulting pidfd; there is no `waitpid`, numeric-PID signal, process scan,
  `Popen` fallback or retry.
- Admission requires one non-inheritable descriptor, stable fdinfo identity,
  exact guardian/broker/worker role, one process/thread owner and an unchanged
  absolute deadline. Initial non-consuming `waitid(P_PIDFD)` plus pidfd poll
  proves that an already-exited child is not returned as live.
- Termination is one-shot `pidfd_send_signal(SIGKILL)`. A
  `ProcessLookupError` is only a race indication; an observed and consumed
  `waitid(P_PIDFD)` event is still required before reap is claimed.
- Reap performs a non-consuming observation followed by one matching consuming
  event. It accepts only the bound child and valid exit/killed/dumped shapes.
  Only a normal status-zero exit satisfies success; abnormal exit can be
  consumed for cleanup without claiming success.
- Close is allowed only after reap. The stored descriptor is revoked before
  its final identity check, so descriptor replacement is not closed and an
  ambiguous close can never be retried.
- Failed initial admission performs bounded terminate, actual consuming reap
  and close when identity remains known. Uncertain cleanup fails closed as
  `cleanup_unconfirmed`.
- Snapshots expose only role and aggregate counts/booleans—no PID, pidfd,
  fdinfo identity, raw exit event or exception text.

## Verification

**878 unique tests pass on CPython 3.11.15 and 3.13.7**, with no failures,
errors or skips: 21 new child-lifecycle tests plus the previous 857
regressions. All pidfd-open, identity, waitid, poll, signal, clock and close
boundaries in the new tests are synthetic.

Syntax/AST checks pass for the two new files on both runtimes; maximum line
length is 89 and trailing whitespace is zero. Tests used `-B`, and no bytecode
file for the new component is present. The five predecessor-plan bindings and
all six new-plan bindings match their recorded sizes and SHA-256 values.

