## Exact next work and unchanged boundary

The next successor must implement the actual fully doubled private composition
over the frozen topology and this child owner: controller forks and pidfd-binds
guardian; guardian adopts its prefork topology, creates the lease, forks and
pidfd-binds broker and worker; every process closes down to its exact final
descriptor set. Cleanup must use only these pidfd owners.

After that, one fixed controller event loop must verify READY before guardian
arm, reserve aggregate bytes and receive ACK before each broker CONTINUE,
verify CONSUMED, collect terminal reports, and enforce the absolute cleanup
deadline. Listener/drop/seal/full-size bootstrap integration and a separately
authorized Linux native qualification still follow.

GPU is still unnecessary. No S3 or other remote availability check was made.
Real import, training and production remain disabled. The new source, test and
three records are local and untracked; nothing was staged, committed or pushed.
